    "title": "Recall Alert: Popular Brand of Cinnamon Being Recalled in Michigan - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Nathan Vandenburg ,\n4 hours ago\nDo you have any cinnamon in your spice rack? If you do, you may want to check on it, because many retailers here in the state of Michigan are recalling certain ground cinnamon brands because of elevated possibilities of lead.\nWhich Cinnamon Brands Are Recalled The FDA found that multiple brands of popular cinnamon, such as La Frontera, Supreme, Tradition, Marcum and others had contained elevated levels of lead. No illnesses have been reported at this time involving the recall, but the possibility of being exposed to lead can be dangerous for anyone, including the young, elderly, or pregnant.\nHealth Risks of Lead Exposure Lead may not always have immediate onset symptoms either . Over time, it can harm the brain, kidneys, or even your nervous system. If you believe that you have any of the affected brands, you should toss them immediately, or return them to the place of purchase for a full refund.\nThis hasn’t been the first spice contamination this year either. ALB Flavor ground cinnamon was recalled earlier last year, after finding that ground cinnamon contained led in some bags sold at Michigan stores.\nSpices are often easy to miss, as the expiration date isn’t as quick as other items.\nWhat You Should Do Now If you know that you have cinnamon inside of your cabinets, you should check them immediately, and see if you can match any of the affected recall products. If you do have them, you should discard of them immediately. If you use your own containers too, you should rinse and wipe them, and not mix them with other spices.\nIf you also experience any headaches, digestive troubles, or fatigue, it may not be a bad idea to bring that up with your doctor.\nItems Currently Under Recall at Michigan Walmart Stores & Walmart.com Items currently being recalled include celery, tires, toys, and more sold at Walmart stores in Michigan and online at Walmart.com. Gallery Credit: George McIntyre Canva Celery Sticks 4 in/1.6 oz bundles, Marketside Celery Sticks, due to possible health risk. Details here. Canva Goodyear Tires Cooper Discoverer Stronghold AT tires, size LT275/65R18 Details here. Canva Portable Power Banks Casely Wireless Portable Power Banks, due to fire and burn hazards. Details here. Canva Infant Swings IxDregan Infant swings due to risk of serious injury or death due to suffocation hazard. Details here. Comeonroa Infant Swings due to risk of serious injury or death due to suffocation hazard. Details here.\nCanva Various Toy Items Multifunctional Puzzle Crab Toy Details here. Fisher-Price Brunch & Go Stroller Toy due to choking hazard. Details here. Fisher-Price Tissue Box Toy sold with SnugaPuppy Activity Center due to choking hazard. Details here. Canva Kentfield Dressers Kentfield Dressers due to risk of serious injury or death due to tipping hazard. Details here. Canva INSE Cordless Stick Vacuums INSE Cordless Stick Vacuums recalled due to fire and burn hazards. Details here.",
